From 1a7a1cefeecc76da38b2ed125619e21629fd4a69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Britten <11667518+marcbritten@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:59:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(project): ask or refuse before a save writes over a
 changed project file

A save to the project's own file now checks the file on disk first. The
project keeps a disk stamp of the file (path, size, modification time)
from the open and from each save. If the stamp is different at the next
save, another window, program or person changed the file.

- The window holds the save and asks: Save As, Cancel or Overwrite.
  Nothing is written before the answer.
- cam.save and the MCP tool save_project refuse by name. They write when
  the caller gives overwrite: true.
- An agent attached to the window uses the window's stamp and gives the
  new stamp back, so the window does not ask about the agent's own save.

A save to another path, a new document and a deleted file are not
checked. New and Open drop a held save. project::save, the file format
and PROJECT_VERSION do not change.

Decisions: docs/decisions/3608-save-overwrite-guard.md.

Fixes #3608

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
